{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327084-shard-world-idea-the-hedge-consumes-the-world","id":327084,"title":"[Shard/World Idea] The Hedge Consumes the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-01T09:01:56-08:00","id":327084,"title":"[Shard/World Idea] The Hedge Consumes the World","content":"Just a story idea I had, inspired by something Raygungothic(sorry if I wrote your name wrong!) said in a thread on the general nWOD section. Basically, it's what is says on the tin. Something happens, and the Hedge surges forth to consume the world. Major collections of human population might remain relatively untouched, if surrounded on all sides, while smaller towns and cities might become Hollows or simply be trapped in the Hedge. How might people(and Them) react? How might government change? How would the Courts react? Other supernaturals(besides, of course, the general cry of &quot;Gently Caress the Acanthus!&quot;)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 12-01-2014, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T10:42:49-08:00","id":327177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327084-shard-world-idea-the-hedge-consumes-the-world#post327084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... the generally cry of &quot;Gently Caress the Acanthus!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well when Onyx Path/CCP authorizes the creation of porn, I know what I'm writing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T16:34:22-08:00","id":327482,"title":"","content":"So, any thoughts? At the very least, I imagine the Templetes might step out of the shadows. Changeling Courts offering their protection for Glamour, Vampire Princes creating true fiefdoms, and packs of the Pure offering Wolfbloods a promise of a &quot;safe place&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T16:40:34-08:00","id":327485,"title":"","content":"End of the World is more likely to occur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:53:13-08:00","id":327656,"title":"","content":"It depends on just how much the Hedge takes over. Assuming the Hedge utterly and completely takes over Earth and makes it like itself, a lot would change.<br /> <br /> Vampires would probably be the most unpredictably affected. Between bloodroots, other goblin fruits, and the strange properties of hedge beasts it might be possible to find a substitute for the vampire\u2019s bloodlust, suppress the Beast, or even make them human again. It will also be easier for vampires to travel and walk about (especially low Humanity vamps) since time won\u2019t flow like it used to.<br /> <br /> The werewolves will suffer a lot. Death rage and lethal damage while off the path will likely cause a great many to die in the immediate aftermath. All spirits (and ghosts for that matter) will be made manifest and start the slow process of turning into hedge beasts. There will probably be a mad rush by some trying to become bound into fetishes rather than have their nature corrupted. Then there\u2019s the lack of essence as the holy spots lose their connection to the spirit world. Of course, eating changelings still provides an easy supply of essence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> In all likelihood the werewolves will nearly all be killed or be driven mad. Fairly appropriate given the balance of a world consumed by the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Mages probably fare the best of the other splats. Of all of them, mages have the best chance of affecting the Hedge around them and manipulating things to their advantage. Aside from changelings they are probably some of the few that can create Hollow. At the same time, going off the path into the soul shredding Thorns holds much greater risks. Do it enough time and the Mage will likely start to lose the ability to work magic. Not to mention the reliability of all perception magic is greatly hindered.<br /> <br /> Changelings (and Tokens and everything else) lose their Mask. If they aren\u2019t killed or driven away because of misplaced blame, they will likely be the saviors of their communities. They have the most experience with Hedge and the Fae. They can provide Hollows and knowledge and protection. Of course, it\u2019s likely none will have Clarity higher than 5. Fetches would be an odd case. They would still be impossible to tell from human, even more so now that sociopathic behavior would be more common. However, with no reason to keep up appearance it would seem the Fae would be less likely to leave a fetch behind. Plus without the toxic nature of Earth to prevent casual visits, the Fair Folk will probably be abducting more people than they used to.<br /> <br /> Overall I\u2019d say things would be pretty bad. The only communities would be those that have changelings or mages to maintain Hollows and keep people from being forced off the path. Those without these protectors would have to be nomads along the Trods and Paths in the ever changing landscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T04:33:13-08:00","id":328046,"title":"","content":"Seems the WoD version of the rpg &quot;Summerland&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static2.paizo.com/image/product/catalog/PSICB/PSICB6400_500.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T05:39:07-08:00","id":328074,"title":"","content":"@Raistlin: Huh, never heard about it. Any mention for what it's about?<br /> <br /> @TrickyBoots: Thanks for commenting! Did not know about the spirit into Hedge Beast thing. Yeah, what few remain are probably gonna stick to the cities, if only because those are the only places with spirit ecologies anymore. The Pure, especially Predator Kings, probably have the highest death count, to be sure.<br /> <br /> As for the less mainstream templates;<br /> <br /> \u2022Sin-Eaters: Depends on wether or not the whole Spirits into Hedge Beast thing happens to ghosts.If so, a lot of the Bound are out of jobs unless they move to or are in the city. Never the less, the fact they're relatively potent, supernatural wise, makes it look like they'd be relatively popular, though I'm not sure how the Hedge affects them. <br /> <br /> \u2022Prometheans: Might not care that much. Sure, while it might make the Pilgrimage more dangerous in some ways, in others, it's a downright boon. After all(though this may be wrong), Arcadia and the Hedge don't hate the Created the way the cruel earth did. And even if they can make Wastelands, the Ulgan's grows rather toothless once the Spirits are gone. The facts that Hobgoblins are probably immune to Disquiet probably make it even more appealing. Still not sure how the Hedge affects them, officially. <br /> <br /> Not sure how other supernaturals might react.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T17:39:31-08:00","id":330652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327084-shard-world-idea-the-hedge-consumes-the-world#post327084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Gently Caress the Acanthus!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a Something Awful buff, aren't you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:08:41-08:00","id":330680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327084-shard-world-idea-the-hedge-consumes-the-world?p=330652#post330652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a Something Awful buff, aren't you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Just Read some FATAL and Friends reviews, I'm afraid. So, any thoughts on the idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T20:52:58-08:00","id":330743,"title":"","content":"I can imagine one truly bizarre occurrence; the alliance of those fallen from the god machine and what remains of the machine and its influences. Oh, just imagine what chaos demons could create for the fae with their own pacts without worry of the machines wrath. Of course sadly some demons would see this as the time to finally destroy the machine and try to join the fae but I feel most would care enough about self preservation to consider that the fae are their true enemy and threat.<br /> <br /> Or allow me to present a side solution depending on your interpretations. Demons allow passage to the shadow and lead an exodus before the hedge cuts them off and hope that the shadow is the safer choice.... what if the shadow ceases to be? what if the hedge reflects a more twisted and dangerous shadow?<br /> <br /> BTW thank you now I am just imagining an GM Demon bargaining with the infernal Demons to more or less open a gate to pour the infernal into this hedge consumed world that the PCs would have to worry about too. Because when it is the end of the world everyone wants to join.<br /> <br /> Edit: no idea how but I thought I was on the main forum sorry for DtD focus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T01:48:57-08:00","id":330913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327084-shard-world-idea-the-hedge-consumes-the-world?p=328046#post328046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems the WoD version of the rpg &amp;quot;Summerland&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static2.paizo.com/image/product/catalog/PSICB/PSICB6400_500.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the heads-up; this looks incredible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T05:39:54-08:00","id":331009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327084-shard-world-idea-the-hedge-consumes-the-world?p=330743#post330743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: no idea how but I thought I was on the main forum sorry for DtD focus</div> </div> </div> </div> No problem at all! Thoughts on this whole idea are fine; I posted it here because it's a primarily Changeling sort of thing, but how anyone might react is always welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}